86045417 true] [17592186443590 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The product of four and a number.\"" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443590 1072 #uuid "0862ccf2-3e10-5094-975a-42a295ffb059" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443590 1074 "If we denote our number by $x,$ then the phrase \"the product of four and a number\" can be written as $4$ times $x,$ or $4x.$" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443591 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443589 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443591 1069 "q-184019" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443591 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443591 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"thirty times a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $w$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443591 1072 #uuid "0fe7bcd3-7cd1-50cd-9437-d695815bcbc1" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443591 1074 "If we denote our number by $w$, then \"thirty times a number\" can be written as\n$30w.$" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443592 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443583 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443592 1069 "q-21507" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443592 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443592 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The product of a number and $3$ more than that same number.\"" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443592 1072 #uuid "3ea89b3c-9f8b-5438-991d-002242e75061" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443592 1074 "If we denote our number by $a$, then ''$3$ more than that number'' can be written as\n\n$$\n3+a.\n$$\n\nSo, the whole phrase can be written as\n\n$$\na\\cdot (3+a).\n$$" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443593 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443584 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443593 1069 "q-27483" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443593 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443593 1071 "The algebraic expression $4w-3$ can be translated into a sentence as" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443593 1072 #uuid "4b801c4c-53a9-5277-82f6-60fd8ea8ed73" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443593 1074 "The first term of the expression is $4w$ and this can be written as \"four times a number\".\n\nSince we have the subtraction $4w-3$, the whole expression can be written as \"the difference between four times a number and three\"." 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443594 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443582 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443594 1069 "q-21264" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443594 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443594 1071 "Translate the phrase \"one-quarter of a number minus three-sevenths of another number\" into an algebraic expression." 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443594 1072 #uuid "5efd65b1-9dc8-5a12-83d6-fd8f864d64db" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443594 1074 "If we denote our first number by $x$ and our second number by $y$, then we can write \"one-quarter of a number \" as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}x\n$$\n\nand \"three-sevenths of a second number\" as\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{7}y.\n$$\n\nSo, the whole sentence is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{3}{7}y.\n$$" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443595 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443585 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443595 1069 "q-184029" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443595 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443595 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"A quarter of a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $y$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443595 1072 #uuid "74b51296-c7b7-5c19-8f08-00846b0aaa79" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443595 1074 "If we denote our number by $y,$ then the phrase can be written as $\\frac{1}{4}y.$" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443596 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443588 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443596 1069 "q-184024" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443596 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443596 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"$20$ minus five times a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $w$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443596 1072 #uuid "7e58b785-f5f2-5a07-a9a0-a68f78076577" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443596 1074 "If we denote our number by $w$, then \"five times a number'' can be written as\n\n$$\n5w.\n$$\n\nSo, the whole phrase can be written as\n\n$$\n20-5w.\n$$" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443597 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443587 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443597 1069 "q-171407" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443597 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443597 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"Two-thirds of a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $k$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443597 1072 #uuid "9993235d-0a25-5a28-9986-8e8c61052303" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443597 1074 "If we denote our number by $k,$ then the phrase can be written as $\\frac{2}{3}k.$" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443598 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443580 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443598 1069 "q-54498" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443598 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443598 1071 "Write \"the quotient of a number and three\" as an algebraic expression." 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443598 1072 #uuid "cc4c452a-9b60-579e-b407-bfc2250db098" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443598 1074 "\"The quotient of a number and three\" means the same thing as \"a number divided by three.\" \n\nIf we call our number $n$, then we can express this mathematically as $\\frac{n}{3}.$" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443599 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443586 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443599 1069 "q-184026" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443599 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443599 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The quotient of twenty and a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $h$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443599 1072 #uuid "e410a5c3-45c2-5472-8881-f44191caa0a7" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true] [17592186443599 1074 "If we denote our number by $h,$ we can write \"the quotient of twenty and a number\" as $\\frac{20}{h}.$" 13194139534905 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-04502abf-d30a-536a-91df-b4f259198cbc" 17592186443550 "answer-098a42b2-f9f6-59cf-8afe-73f54612025a" 17592186443551 "answer-14207910-bc3d-5531-8c71-def14534c5c9" 17592186443552 "answer-1c85e377-c6c4-5da5-9c0b-11a2bd86cad2" 17592186443553 "answer-20a7d5c1-5cae-5ede-9f9f-7716fe5947a5" 17592186443554 "answer-2a061b4e-158c-520a-b680-e0da5839969a" 17592186443555 "answer-2ef752e3-0e4a-5804-8722-db9aefd92aec" 17592186443556 "answer-3468384a-6f60-5d04-8eeb-ade9d4813b73" 17592186443557 "answer-3f270e25-1288-5f92-b0f6-e5f4bf94749e" 17592186443558 "answer-412e16b1-8ba1-5a29-bbd9-ec7f116405e2" 17592186443559 "answer-43f95ef4-a07d-56e1-83a5-99f832e76e80" 17592186443560 "answer-482e8af7-a8f0-5157-9046-9e67b67879af" 17592186443561 "answer-557a9c23-0600-5707-b994-9ece61fe6761" 17592186443562 "answer-5b83cfee-994d-5f59-b465-9fd29c83501d" 17592186443563 "answer-728d7016-49b3-5b55-963c-475ca552a